  "title": "TRY OVERSHARING YOUR JOY",
  "period": "August 13–16",
  "passages": [
    "I began writing more directly about joy. Share the ridiculous, beautiful things. Dress boldly. Dance. Make the entrance. Let people see what fills your cup.",
    "There was a lemon-party outfit made from materials sourced through a friend. There were rooms full of creative people. Tamarack's crew took first at the Bluewater Regatta. These moments mattered because joy had people in it. I wanted to celebrate the friends who joined the dance, matched the energy, and helped make the experience possible."
  ],
  "reflections": [
    {
      "kind": "Notice",
      "prompt": "What joy have you been keeping small?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "Write",
      "prompt": "Name a recent joy and a person who helped make it possible. How would you like to celebrate it?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "Try",
      "prompt": "Choose how to celebrate: enjoy the moment privately, make something from it, or share it with someone you trust."
    }
  ],
